      "completedAt": "2026-09-11T16:05:40.000Z",
      "conclusion": "Nine-task information-sufficiency evaluation found Strata insufficient on 3 of 9 where raw DDL was sufficient: inspect omitted unique constraints, check constraints and indexes, all already in the model and populated by introspection but never rendered. Fixed; now 9/9. Repair cost ~141 tokens across 7 tasks (ratio 2.4x to 2.3x), establishing that the context reduction reported in EV-STRATA-2026-F4C6 is genuine rather than an artefact of dropping data. Task set was author-written, which biases toward questions Strata answers well; only inspect was probed in depth. Still not agent correctness."
    },
    {
      "id": "WI-0023",
      "type": "research",
      "state": "complete",
      "semanticState": "complete",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "type": "research-record",
          "path": "research/evidence/EV-STRATA-2026-D8E1--agent-correctness-null-result.md"
        }
      ],
      "updatedAt": "2026-09-11T16:19:15.000Z",
      "telemetryExecutionIds": [
        "EXE-20260911T161752463Z-6dd5fbac"
      ],
      "completedAt": "2026-09-11T16:19:15.000Z",
      "conclusion": "Six agents, three per condition, identical graded task set. NULL RESULT: 15/15 correct in both conditions, no difference detected, and the Strata condition used 8.7% more tokens. Ceiling effect - an 8KB context is small enough that a capable agent misses nothing, including the designed discriminator. HY-STRATA-2026-2A6F tested and not supported, remains proposed rather than rejected. HY-STRATA-2026-1E5D qualified: it holds for large schemas with targeted queries and is actively false for small schemas with pre-fetched sessions. The crossover schema size is now the largest decision-relevant unknown."
    }
